# Android movie watchlist
Kotlin, Jetpack Compose, Material 3, single module, minSdk 26.

## Stack (nothing else without asking)
Room (KSP), Retrofit + kotlinx.serialization, Coil, Navigation Compose, Jetpack DataStore, coroutines/Flow, ViewModel.
No Hilt. Wire dependencies manually with one AppContainer created in the Application class.
In-app browser = WebView via AndroidView.

## Build rules
Do not add or upgrade dependencies, or change Gradle/AGP/Kotlin/KSP versions, without asking. Use the version catalog (libs.versions.toml).
Use current, non-deprecated Compose APIs.
Use the Gradle wrapper for this OS: gradlew.bat on Windows, ./gradlew otherwise.
Finish all edits for a feature, then run assembleDebug and fix errors. Before calling a feature done, also run lintDebug and testDebugUnitTest.
If the same build error persists after 2 attempts, stop and show me the full error instead of retrying.

## Data
Source: TMDB v3 (https://api.themoviedb.org/3). Send the key as the api_key query parameter.
The key is entered by the user at runtime and stored in DataStore. Never hardcode a key. Never create a BuildConfig key.
Poster URL: https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342 + poster_path.
Room table "movies": tmdbId (primary key), imdbId, title, year, shortDescription, posterUrl, addedAt.
shortDescription = tagline if not blank, else overview.
The list reads only from Room, ordered by addedAt DESC (newest at top, oldest at bottom).
Ignore duplicate adds.

## UI rules
Tiles: full width, rounded corners (16.dp), 12.dp padding, height from content. The "+" tile is shorter, same shape, only a + icon.
The About screen shows: This product uses the TMDB API but is not endorsed or certified by TMDB.
Never use Modifier.blur or RenderEffect. Any blur must be done in app code (software) and work on all API levels.
Configure Coil with allowHardware(false) so images can be captured to a bitmap.

## Safety
Never read or edit keystores, *.jks, google-services.json, or local.properties.
Do not run git commands other than git status and git diff.
Keep NOTES.md updated with decisions and current status.